# Version 9 · the fall of the temple as the frame story
title: Do Not Be Afraid
subtitle: Version 9 · Not One Stone
tempo: 98
key: G minor
music: epic
intensity: 0.95
grade: ember
images: ../assets/img/{}-2.webp
endnote: "Here I am! I stand at the door and knock."
endref: Revelation 3:20

@0:00-0:02 black cue:drone,0.6
sfx: riser
@0:02-0:05 img:stone ken:push hit:2
title: 70 AD
@0:05-0:12 img:ruins ken:left cue:tense,0.6
vo: The greatest building in the world, burning.
vo: "Not one stone will be left on another."
ref: Matthew 24:2
@0:12-0:17 img:jerusalem ken:slow cue:drone,0.5
vo: Forty years earlier, He had warned them. And wept.
@0:17-0:19 drop:"The light shines in the darkness" ref:"John 1:5"
@0:19-0:25 img:child ken:up grade:dawn cue:wonder,0.9
vo: It began with love.
vo: Before anything was made, there was love.
@0:25-0:30 img:steps ken:down fx:flare grade:dawn
vo: Not a little. Not enough.
+2 title: Overflowing
@0:30-0:36 img:turn ken:in grade:dawn
vo: For the lost. For the misguided.
vo: For the ones who would wound Him.
@0:36-0:40 img:smile ken:still hold:silent grade:dawn
@0:40-0:46 img:hands ken:slow fx:dove grade:dawn cue:wonder,1
vo: Nothing you do to the body can touch what He holds.
@0:46-0:52 img:kneel ken:in cue:tense,0.8
vo: "Whoever causes one of these little ones to stumble..."
ref: Matthew 18:6
@0:52-0:57 img:millstone ken:down
vo: "...better for them to have a millstone hung around their neck."
@0:57-1:03 img:door ken:push cue:tense,1
vo: "I never knew you."
ref: Matthew 7:23
@1:03-1:05 drop:"I am the way, the truth and the life" ref:"John 14:6"
@1:05-1:09 img:temple ken:right cue:build
vo: In the temple courts, they sold, and bargained, and shut people out.
@1:09-1:13 img:take ken:in
text: Our struggle is not / against flesh and blood.
ref: Ephesians 6:12
@1:13-1:17 cuts:cords,knot,knot!,eyes,braid,whip cue:war
text: He made a whip of cords.
ref: John 2:15
@1:17-1:22 img:tables ken:slow hit:2
vo: "...and drove them all out of His Father's house."
@1:22-1:27 img:doves ken:up fx:flare cue:choir
text: We do not fight people.
text: We fight for them.
@1:27-1:31 img:whipfloor ken:still cue:choir,0.6
title: Love is not weak.
@1:31-1:33 drop:"Take heart. I have overcome the world." ref:"John 16:33"
@1:33-1:41 img:weep ken:slow cue:weep
vo: He wept over the city,
vo: because it did not recognize the time of God's coming.
ref: Luke 19:41–44
# back to the frame
@1:41-1:43 img:stone ken:push hit:2
@1:43-1:49 img:ruins ken:right cue:tense,0.7
vo: Stones fall. Empires fall.
+3 title: What He holds does not.
@1:49-1:54 img:redsea ken:in cue:drone,0.8
sfx: braam
vo: "The Lord will fight for you."
ref: Exodus 14:14
@1:54-2:06 img:grown ken:in cue:heart
text: I will not fear.
text: Fear makes the soul small.
text: Let it come. / Let it pass through me.
text: Only He remains.
@2:06-2:13 img:stand ken:up fx:rise cue:tutti grade:dawn
vo: "Do not fear, for I am with you...
vo: I will uphold you with my righteous right hand."
ref: Isaiah 41:10
@2:13-2:16 img:dawn ken:push hit:2 grade:dawn
title: So stand.
@2:16-2:21 img:opendoor ken:in fade cue:outro grade:dawn
text: You were never forced.
text: You were invited.
@2:21-2:26 black
title: Do not be afraid.
